From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: H. M. Yousuf <hmyousuf@nirapod.org>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:05:23 +0600
Subject: [PATCH] jasmin2ec: the safety model

jasmin2ec -m safety extracts a model whose procedures carry the safety
conditions of the program as assertions: the assertions come from the
safety pass (Safety.sc_prog) after default contracts are added (array
parameters and results initialised). Initialisation is made explicit by
masks (safety_mask.ml): a boolean per scalar and a byte array per array
(0xFF where a cell is initialised), passed with array arguments and
returned with array results, including results written to a sub-array.
The model records a trace of the assertions in each procedure and, with
--output-proof, emits one <f>_spec Hoare lemma per contract with a proof
skeleton. The pass is extracted from the proofs (proofs/lang/extraction.v)
and runs in compile.ml before the extraction to EasyCrypt. The masks are
hand-written OCaml, outside the proofs, like the rest of the extraction to
EasyCrypt.
